# Datasets (downloaded / derived — too large for git)
dataset/fedcond_qa/
dataset/fedcond_qa_medical_backup/

# dataset/linearrag/{hotpotqa,musique,2wikimultihop}/{chunks,questions}.json
# are intentionally TRACKED (like dataset/raw/ below): all three are now
# built by scripts/setup_datasets.py from the same fixed 1000-question
# HippoRAG benchmark split, so committing them means a fresh clone needs no
# extra dataset-build step for the main training pipeline either.

# dataset/raw/ (hotpotqa/musique/2wikimultihopqa + corpora, ~41MB) is
# intentionally TRACKED, not ignored: it's the exact HippoRAG paper
# benchmark data (see scripts/setup_datasets.py), committed so baseline
# comparisons stay reproducible even if upstream's reproduce/dataset/
# changes later. Used only by fedcond_grag/baselines/* -- not the main
# FedCondGraphRAG training pipeline (that uses dataset/linearrag/*).

